@startuml
title Protocol Emulator ASIC — planned architecture
top to bottom direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

package "Demo host / board" {
  component "Linux PC\nDemo host GUI (planned)" as pc
  component "Tiny Tapeout demo board\nRP2040 controller (Raspberry Pi Pico)" as board
  component "Protocol wires" as wires
}

package "Tiny Tapeout top" {
  component "Passive SPI loader\npe_ctrl" as loader
  package "Loader readback A1 — landed 2026-09-24 (R1 framed bus supersedes the raw echo)" {
    component "Host response bus\nuio[6] MISO frame; commit-latched LOAD echo\nR1: uio[4:7] CS_N/MOSI/MISO/SCK" as readback
  }
  package "Programmable SoC — pe_soc" {
    component "CPU\nfirmware engine" as cpu
    component "Instruction SRAM\n1024 × 16" as imem
    component "CPU data memory\n16-byte register array" as dmem
    component "Frame buffer SRAM\n2 KB" as fbuf
    component "Tick timer\n60 MHz timebase" as tick
    component "Pin matrix\nper-pin OUT / OE / IN / OD" as pinmux

    package "Integrated baseline: 10BASE-T receive" {
      component "DRU\noversampled capture" as dru
      component "Manchester decoder" as manch_rx
      component "Ethernet RX MAC" as eth_rx
      component "CRC-32 check" as crc_rx
    }

    package "Integrated shared word engine" {
      component "Indexed control window\nIO port 0xF; 32 entries; 8-bit data" as window
      component "Programmable timing\nencoded-cell strobe + half-cell level + payload enables" as timing
      component "pe_serdes\n32-bit word engine\ntx_bit_en / rx_bit_en (split)" as serdes
      component "pe_codec_mux TX\nrecommended instance\nNRZI / Manchester / stuffing" as codec_tx
      component "pe_codec_mux RX\nrecommended instance\nNRZI / Manchester / stuffing" as codec_rx
      component "Per-pin level overlay\nbefore OE / open-drain gate" as overlay
      component "TX owner mux\ntx_path: SERDES or eth_tx" as tx_mux
    }

    package "Integrated 10BASE-T TX frame path (landed)" {
      component "Frame source\nfirmware pushes bytes via window" as tx_source
      component "Frame + preamble/SFD\npe_eth_tx engine" as tx_frame
      component "TX-dedicated CRC\nFCS field mode" as tx_crc
      component "IFG / transmit control\n96-cell gap; runt/jabber guard; 8-byte FIFO" as tx_control
    }

  }
  component "Pads\nui_in / uo_out / uio\nuo_out[2] = eth_tx (G6)" as pads
}

pc <--> board : host-control link; transport TBD
board --> loader : SPI program load
loader --> imem : host write port
loader ..> readback : A1 word echo; one frame late
readback ..> pads : MISO on uio[4]
wires --> board : optional SPI MISO readback
board --> pc : optional readback / status
imem --> cpu : instruction fetch
cpu <--> dmem : load / store
cpu <--> tick : timed firmware I/O
cpu <--> pinmux : pin-port reads / writes
pinmux <--> pads : levels, enables, inputs
pads <--> wires : board connections, including optional SPI MISO

wires --> dru : 10BASE-T receive
dru --> manch_rx : recovered half-bits
manch_rx --> eth_rx : decoded bits
eth_rx --> crc_rx : received frame
eth_rx --> fbuf : store-and-forward
fbuf --> cpu : firmware frame window

cpu <--> window : indexed control / data
window --> timing : divisor / mode
window --> serdes : data / lengths / control
timing --> codec_tx : encoded-cell strobe + half_phase
timing --> codec_rx : encoded-cell strobe (plain / NRZI / stuffed)
timing --> serdes : tx_bit_en / rx_bit_en (payload-only)
serdes --> codec_tx : TX bits
codec_tx --> serdes : tx_stuffed (hold)
codec_tx --> overlay : encoded TX level
overlay --> pinmux : override level before OE gate
dru --> codec_rx : rx_wire or Manchester halves
dru --> codec_rx : dru.bit_en (Manchester cell strobe)
codec_rx --> serdes : rx_bit / rx_bit_valid (skip stuff cells)

tx_source --> tx_frame : push bytes
tx_frame --> tx_crc : FCS field
tx_crc --> tx_control
tx_control --> tx_mux : 96-cell IFG / frame TX bit
window --> tx_source : push / TXLEN / TXCTRL / TXSTAT (bank 16-27)
serdes --> tx_mux : tx_bit (default owner)
tx_frame --> tx_mux : eth_tx_bit
tx_mux --> codec_tx : owned tx_bit into shared codec
tx_mux --> pads : uo_out[2] eth_tx (G6, behind pin_oe_bus[7])

note bottom of pads
  Baseline firmware personas: UART, SPI master, I2C master.
  The passive loader is a separate SPI path used to load instruction SRAM.
  Current aliases: uo_out[0] is UART TX / SPI SCLK; ui_in[0] is UART RX /
  SPI MISO; uio[0:1] are I2C SDA/SCL; uio[2:3] are SPI MOSI/CS_N.
  ui_in[2] is 10BASE-T RX; uo_out[2] is 10BASE-T TX (G6 reclaim of dbg_pc[0]).
end note

note bottom of pads
  The Linux GUI and its PC-to-board transport are planned software; the
  transport and control API are not chosen yet. The RP2040 sits on the Tiny
  Tapeout demo board and is the chip-side SPI host.
end note

note bottom of pads
  Landed 2026-09-24 (manager decision): the R1 framed host bus supersedes the
  A1 raw uio[4] echo — SPI mode 0, MSB-first 16-bit words, 16'hA55A sync,
  CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE, response opcode bit 7, sequence/target echoed; the
  commit-latched word echo lives in the framed LOAD response. Pads: uio[4:7]
  = CS_N/MOSI/MISO/SCK, uo_out[1] = IRQ_N (sticky, active low), ui_in[3:5]
  freed; 19 of 24 committed. See wiki/plans/host-controller-gui.md and
  wiki/plans/pe-ctrl-readback.
end note

note bottom of pads
  Landed 2026-09-24: ONE pe_serdes with split payload-only enables (TX
  advances only on payload cells, serdes.tx_bit_en = tx_codec_cell_en &&
  !tx_stuffed; RX captures only payload cells, serdes.rx_bit_en =
  rx_codec_cell_en && rx_bit_valid). TWO unmodified pe_codec_mux instances are
  clocked per encoded cell -- never per half-cell -- and half_phase is an
  independent 2x half-cell LEVEL; the pad overlay sits before the matrix's
  open-drain gate, and a latched-phase window on port 0xF has
  separate TXLEN/RXLEN. First consumer is the wire loopback (plain and stuffed
  Manchester, word 0x07E0) through TX codec, simulation wire model, DRU/codec
  RX, and SERDES RX; a trailing stuff cell is covered by construction. The
  10BASE-T TX frame consumer (pe_eth_tx) is integrated below and shares the
  TX codec through the tx_path owner mux. Landed 2026-09-25 (plan Tasks 1-5):
  full frame from firmware pushes, 32-entry window, owner mux, G6 uo_out[2]
  pad, loopback acceptance PASS (FCS 9cc5cb34, IFG 102 cells). Plan Tasks 6
  (mutation suites) and 7 (STA + closeout) remain OPEN.
  Low-speed USB and CAN are later personas; JTAG, SWD, and PS/2 are optional.
  Evidence: reviews/2026-09-24/SERDES-INTEGRATION-REVIEW.md.
end note


@enduml
